"The input prompt goes through tokenization (splitting into tokens), then embedding (converting tokens into numerical vectors), then the Transformer processes these vectors using (self-attention) 
to understand context, and finally generates a response through next-token prediction — this whole process is called LLM inference."

Text → Tokens → Token IDs (numbers) → Embedding vectors (meaning as numbers) → Transformer processes these vectors → predicts next token → repeats to generate a response.

Step 1: Tokenization (breaking your sentence into pieces)

Your prompt "What is machine learning" gets split into tokens — not always whole words, sometimes sub-words or even single characters, depending on the tokenizer used.

"What is machine learning"
        ↓
["What", " is", " machine", " learning"]

Important nuance: the diagram simplifies it. Tokens aren't always clean whole words like shown. For example:

"understanding" might become:
["under", "stand", "ing"]

This is because the tokenizer (like BPE — Byte Pair Encoding) breaks text into common sub-word chunks, so it can handle ANY word (even made-up ones) without needing every possible word pre-defined.

------------------------------------------------------------

Step 2: Token → Number (Token ID)

Each token gets mapped to a fixed number from the model's vocabulary (a lookup table built during training):

"What"      → 4013
" is"       → 318
" machine"  → 4572
" learning" → 6509

------------------------------------------------------------

Step 3: Number → Embedding Vector

(This is what the diagram shows as [0.23, -0.45, 1.20...])

Each Token ID gets converted into a vector — a list of hundreds/thousands of numbers that represent that word's meaning in mathematical space (similar to what you did with nomic-embed-text in your RAG project).

"What" → [0.23, -0.45, 1.20, ...]
         (e.g., 768 or 4096 numbers, depending on model size)

------------------------------------------------------------

Step 4: "Real LLM starts working"

This is the Transformer processing these vectors through many layers, using self-attention (figuring out which words relate to which other words), ultimately predicting the next token, converting it back to a word, and repeating.

-------------------------------------------

Breaking down each specific step's name:

+---------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Step                                                          | Name of the process                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Text → Tokens (breaking sentence into pieces)                 | Tokenization                                                   |
|                                                               |                                                               |
| Token → Token ID (number lookup)                              | Encoding (or "vocabulary lookup")                             |
|                                                               |                                                               |
| Token ID → Vector of numbers                                  | Embedding (specifically, this creates a "token embedding"      |
|                                                               | or "word embedding")                                          |
|                                                               |                                                               |
| Vectors flowing through Transformer layers,                   | Self-Attention (the core mechanism of the Transformer          |
| understanding relationships between words                     | architecture)                                                 |
|                                                               |                                                               |
| Final vector → Predicting the next token                      | Decoding (or "generation")                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Neural Network (the overall structure)
   └── Transformer architecture (a specific TYPE of neural network)
         └── Self-Attention (the KEY mechanism INSIDE the Transformer)

Precise breakdown:

+------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Component        | What it is                                                                                  |
+------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Neural Network   | The broad category — layers of interconnected "neurons" (nodes) that process numbers.      |
|                  |                                                                                             |
| Transformer      | A specific type of neural network architecture, invented in 2017, built specifically        |
|                  | around self-attention.                                                                      |
|                  |                                                                                             |
| Self-Attention   | The specific mechanism inside the Transformer that lets the model figure out which words    |
|                  | in a sentence relate to each other, and how strongly.                                       |
+------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
